.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dsa
trains the recognition half of competitive programming: deciding
.I which
pattern a problem needs when nothing tells you.
It is a spaced\-repetition game, not a problem archive.
.PP
A problem statement is never shown with its pattern named.
You commit to an answer first; only then does the program explain what gave it
away, and which cue you missed.
.PP
Three abilities are tracked and scheduled independently, because they decay at
different rates.
You can keep recognising a pattern long after you have lost the ability to
write
one, and a single mastery number hides exactly that.
.RS 4
.TP 18
.B recognition
Name the pattern from an unlabelled statement.
.TP
.B recall
Given the name, produce its signals, invariant, complexity and template.
.TP
.B implementation
Write correct C++ under time.
.RE
.PP
All C++ you submit is compiled and executed inside a sandbox.
The application works offline; nothing is transmitted anywhere.
.
.SH INSTALLATION
.nf
uv tool install --editable .
.fi
.PP
This places
.B dsa
in
.I ~/.local/bin
so it runs from any directory.
If the shell reports
.BR "command not found" ,
that directory is not on your
.BR PATH :
.PP
.nf
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
.fi
.PP
A plain
.B uv pip install -e .
sets up a development environment for running the tests. It does
.I not
put
.B dsa
on your PATH; the executable stays at
.I .venv/bin/dsa
and only works inside the project directory.
.PP
Confirm the installation with
.BR "dsa doctor" .
.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B dsa
With no command, launch the interactive campaign map.
.TP
.B dsa practice
Run a session chosen by the scheduler: due reviews first, then your weakest
started patterns, then new material.
.TP
.B dsa review
Run a session containing only cards that are due.
.TP
.B dsa stats
Print level, XP, streak, per\-pattern mastery, your most common confusions,
your
most common mistakes, and what to practise next.
.TP
.B dsa patterns
Print every pattern with its mastery bar and lock state.
.TP
.B dsa pattern \fIPATTERN_ID\fR
Print one pattern's signals, anti\-signals, confusions, invariant, complexity
and common mistakes.
.TP
.B dsa streak
Print the current and best daily streak.
.TP
.B dsa doctor
Check the sandbox, the toolchain, the editor, the content tree and the
database.
Run this first if anything misbehaves.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --db " PATH"
Use an alternative progress database. Default: see \fBFILES\fR.
.TP
.BI --size " N" ", " -n " N"
Number of exercises in the session. Default 8 for
.BR practice ,
12 for
.BR review .
.TP
.B --template
For
.BR "dsa pattern" :
print the pattern's canonical C++ template with syntax highlighting instead of
its prose entry.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage for the command and exit.
.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
Bindings in the interactive interface.
.SS Campaign map
.TP 14
.B p
Start a practice session.
.TP
.B r
Start a review session (due cards only).
.TP
.B t
Train under a master, or open the journey map when none is teaching.
.TP
.B d
Start a run of Pattern Duels.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SS During a session
.TP 14
.B 1 2 3 4
Answer a Pattern Hunter question with option A, B, C or D.
.TP
.B space
Advance to the next exercise after reading the feedback.
.TP
.B ctrl+s
Submit a Code Completion answer for judging. In a boss fight this opens the
understanding check first; the code is captured before the questions are asked.
.TP
.B enter
Move to the next field of an understanding check, and commit from the last.
.TP
.B escape
Abandon the session and return to the map.
.TP
.B ctrl+q
Quit the application from anywhere.
.
.SH GAME MODES
.TP
.B Pattern Hunter
An unlabelled statement and four patterns. Distractors are drawn from the
correct pattern's confusion graph and ordered by how often you personally have
made that exact mistake, so your own wrong answers make later rounds harder.
Trains \fBrecognition\fR.
.TP
.B Code Completion
A canonical template with its load\-bearing lines removed. Your answer is
judged
differentially against the intact template, so there is no authored answer key
to disagree with the code. Trains \fBimplementation\fR.
.TP
.B Pattern Recall
Cued recall of a pattern's structure, self\-graded against a rubric whose
essential points cannot be waved through. Trains \fBrecall\fR.
.TP
.B Pattern Duel
Two deliberately confusable statements, shown side by side, to separate. Marked
correct only when \fBboth\fR sides are right, so swapping them fails. Assigning
one pattern to both statements is allowed and is reported as a collapse \(em no
discrimination at all. Trains \fBrecognition\fR.
.TP
.B Boss Fight
Unlabelled, multi\-pattern, explain\-then\-implement, behind a mastery gate.
Trains \fBimplementation\fR.
.
.SH UNDERSTANDING CHECK
Before a boss fight's implement phase is judged, three questions are asked:
the key idea, the expected complexity, and the invariant being maintained.
.PP
The order is the mechanism. Your code is captured the moment you press
\fBctrl+s\fR, before the questions appear, so time spent answering cannot
change what is submitted and the verdict cannot inform your reasoning. Code and
reasoning are then graded independently, which is what allows "correct code,
no idea why" to be recorded as exactly that.
.PP
Answers are matched against phrases the pattern's author wrote down. Nothing
here understands English, so a correct answer phrased unusually can be marked
unsound. Because of that a failed check costs nothing: no health, no failed
phase, no lost exercise. It is recorded, and the master says so.
.PP
.nf
UNDERSTANDING CHECK
  key idea + complexity + invariant, asked before judging
  code captured first, so the answers cannot be retrofitted
  graded lexically against the author's accepts phrases
  failing costs no health and fails no phase
  correct code + unsound reasoning = recorded as memorised
.fi
.
.SH VERDICTS
Judge outcomes for a submission.
.TP 8
.B AC
Accepted. Every test passed.
.TP
.B WA
Wrong Answer. Output differs; the first divergence is reported by token index.
.TP
.B TLE
Time Limit Exceeded. Wall clock or CPU budget exhausted.
.TP
.B MLE
Memory Limit Exceeded. Confirmed from the cgroup's OOM counter.
.TP
.B RE
Runtime Error. The likely cause is named (segfault, bad_alloc, division by
zero,
optimised undefined behaviour).
.TP
.B CE
Compilation Error. Sandbox paths are stripped from the log.
.TP
.B OLE
Output Limit Exceeded. The program produced more output than the cap allows.
.TP
.B IE
Judge Error. A sandbox or harness failure. Never counted against you, and
never
recorded as a lapse.
.
