.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check the installation before anything else:
.B dsa doctor
.TP
Twenty minutes of whatever the scheduler thinks you need:
.B dsa practice
.TP
Clear only what is due, worth 1.5x XP:
.B dsa review
.TP
See which patterns you confuse for each other:
.B dsa stats
.TP
Read one pattern's discriminators before a contest:
.B dsa pattern binary-search-answer
.TP
Print a template to study or copy:
.B dsa pattern sliding-window --template
.TP
Keep a throwaway profile for experimenting:
.B dsa practice --db /tmp/scratch.db
.TP
Author your own patterns without touching the installed set:
.B DSAQUEST_CONTENT=~/my-patterns dsa patterns
.
.SH SANDBOX
Submitted C++ is compiled and run under three layers.
.PP
.nf
systemd-run --user --scope    cgroup v2: MemoryMax, MemorySwapMax, TasksMax
  bwrap                       no network, no host filesystem, own PID
namespace
    prlimit                   RLIMIT_CPU, RLIMIT_AS, RLIMIT_FSIZE,
RLIMIT_STACK
      your program
.fi
.PP
Compilation is sandboxed too, not only execution: a C++ compiler is an
interpreter with filesystem access, and GCC's
.B #embed
and
.B __has_include
can otherwise read host files.
.PP
Only
.I /usr
is visible inside the jail, read\-only. There is no
.IR /home ,
no
.IR /etc ,
no network.
.PP
The application refuses to execute C++ at all if the sandbox is unavailable
rather than falling back to unisolated execution.
Run
.B dsa doctor
to see which layers your kernel supports.
.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.TP
.B DSA Quest will not execute C++ without isolation
The kernel or userland is missing a required layer. On Arch:
.B sudo pacman -S bubblewrap util-linux
.TP
.B the reference template does not build or run
A content bug, not yours. The intact template failed, so no answer key could
be
derived. Report it.
.TP
.B database is at schema version N
The database was written by a newer build. Upgrade the application; it will
not
downgrade a database.
.
.SH NOTES
Only
.BR practice ", " review
and the bare
.B dsa
command load the interactive interface.
.BR stats ", " patterns ", " pattern ", " streak " and " doctor
render through a lightweight path and start in roughly a quarter of a second.
.PP
Unlocking a pattern is permanent. If a prerequisite later decays below the
threshold, access already granted is not withdrawn \(em taking it back would
punish you for honestly reporting that you had forgotten something.
.
